# secrets must NEVER enter an image (longterm Dockerfile does COPY . .)
# A bare `.env` matches only the repo root; deploy/langfuse/.env slipped into a 2026-10-28
# build that way (ship_image.sh refused it). `**/` covers every directory.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
*.bak
**/*.bak
# The Langfuse stack is deployed by its own compose file, never from an agent image.
deploy/langfuse/
# local tooling / bulky non-runtime dirs
.claude/
longterm_agent/reports/
# Host Python environments — 154MB of macOS-built binaries that are dead weight inside a
# linux/amd64 image, and paid for again on every push and pull.
.venv/
.conda/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
# Experiment outputs: regenerated by the harness, never read at runtime.
*.csv










